    YMD (DATE_YEAR `the day of the change`) (DATE_MONTH `the day of the change`)
        (`Days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the day of the change`) (DATE_YEAR `the day of the change`))

GIVETH A NUMBER
`special provision 6: the days before the end of the period in which the premium is adjusted` MEANS 30

GIVEN `the day`                    IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`special provision 6: the premium may be adjusted on` `the day` `, the period ending` `the last day of the period` MEANS
        `the day` AT MOST  `the last day of the period`
    AND `the day` AT LEAST (`the last day of the period` MINUS `special provision 6: the days before the end of the period in which the premium is adjusted`)

§§ `7. Premium adjustment and declaration of wages`

-- (a) The premium is based on the number of employees insured and the total wages the
-- policyholder paid them in the period. (b) If those differ from the figures the premium was
-- first based on, the difference is collected or refunded, on the basis that the minimum
-- premium payable is VND1.500.000. (c) The policyholder keeps accurate records and lets the
-- Company inspect them at any time.
-- The premium rate is not in the wording: the premium on the actual figures is an input.
